Fix is correct and small. Centralize in one helper and use it at both sites so the chain stays single-threaded — the portrait must be drawn from the POST-generateDay chain:

function regenAndGreet(next) {
  next = generateDay(next);
  next.phase = "shop";
  const rng = makeRng(next.rngState);   // re-seed from generateDay's advanced state
  setFace(next, rng, "greet", null);
  next.rngState = rng.state;            // persist the portrait draw
  if (next.event) toast(next, `${next.event.title}: ${next.event.text}`);
  return next;
}

Then sleep() lines 464-468 become `return regenAndGreet(next);` and ackBackstory lines 483-487 become `return regenAndGreet(next);`. Note that in sleep(), the line-425 `rng` is then unused on the normal path (it is still used by the early game-over/win/backstory branches at 434/445/460, so keep makeRng at 425). Optionally drop the now-redundant `let next = {...state, rngState: rng.state}` aliasing if the early branches are also refactored. No other call sites need changes — walk, offer, startHaggle, completeBuy/Sell already persist correctly.

